# Concepts are executable documentation; preserve their intentionally instance-oriented handlers.
[concepts/**/*.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1822.severity = none

# CA1822: these control verbs intentionally hang off the current JobContext instance for API fluency.
# CA1062: MapAsync's groupName is validated on entry - IdentifierSyntax.ValidateUserKebab reaches
# EnsureNonEmptyAndLength, which opens with ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(value, nameof(groupName)),
# so a null already throws naming the right parameter before the flagged use. CA1062 does not follow
# validation two frames down, and a local guard would be dead code; the sibling ParallelAsync validates
# the same way and escapes the rule only because it never dereferences the name.
# CA1031: two catches in the release path of RunWithLockAsync<TResult>. The outer one keeps a failed
# lock release from replacing the action's own result or exception - escaping there would turn a
# completed unit of work into a failure over a cleanup step the lease TTL already covers - and reports
# it through OnLockReleaseFailure; the inner bare catch guards that observer and is deliberately silent,
# because a broken observability hook must not alter the outcome either.
# CA1819: SignalWaitOutcome.Value, on the protected record struct WaitSignalCoreAsync returns. It is
# not a property guarding state a caller could reach past - it is the raised slot's stored bytes in
# transit, returned by the subclass sink and handed straight to DeserializeSignalPayload(byte,
# byte[]), which takes byte[] because the serializer registry does. Widening it to ReadOnlyMemory
# would cost a copy at the only two members that ever touch it, and both are on the frozen 1.0.0
# surface: the record struct is protected on the public abstract class handlers receive.
[src/Acta/Execution/JobContext.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1822.severity = none
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1062.severity = none
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1031.severity = none
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1819.severity = none

#### Scoped analyzer rulings ####

# Rulings made per site, one section per file, each carrying the reason that site was cleared. What the
# move out of the source costs is member precision: .editorconfig scopes by path, so a file-level entry
# also switches the rule off for members of that file nobody judged, and for any added afterwards. Each
# section therefore names the members its ruling was made for.

# CA2213: the three fault sources are minted by their Start* verb and owned from then on by the loop it
# launches (RunContinuousCrashesAsync / RunQueuePressureAsync / RunOutboxPressureAsync), which disposes
# each one in its own finally. Dispose here only Cancels: the loop is still awaiting Token when it runs,
# so disposing the source from the field would race that read into ObjectDisposedException instead of
# stopping the fault.
[anvil/Anvil/FaultInjectors.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA2213.severity = none

# CA1050: AnvilServer, the constants holder naming the loopback address the dashboard binds, prints
# and opens. It sits in the global namespace because this file is Anvil's entry point: a file-scoped
# namespace has to precede every other member and top-level statements have to come first, so the two
# cannot share a file, and the brace form is what csharp_style_namespace_declarations = file_scoped
# above rules out. Its only readers are four sites in this same file, and Anvil is the internal
# certification harness with IsPackable false, so the collision with a consumer's own type that
# CA1050 exists to prevent has no consumer to collide with.
[anvil/Anvil/Program.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1050.severity = none

# CA2000: Spawn's Process is not lost - ownership passes to the ManagedWorker parked in _workers, and
# every exit from that dictionary disposes it: Snapshot() disposes the entries it evicts past the
# retention window, Dispose() the survivors, and the Start() failure path disposes before rethrowing.
# CA2000 cannot follow the handoff through the dictionary.
[anvil/Anvil/WorkerProcessLauncher.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA2000.severity = none

# CA1062: the Write side of the three hand-written ref converters. System.Text.Json owns the call and
# never hands a converter a null writer, so the guard is reachable only by invoking the converter
# directly instead of through the serializer. The code-generated converters in the same assembly emit
# the identical unguarded one-line body for this shape, so a throw in these three alone would put them
# out of step with the generator for no reachable gain.
[src/Acta/{Alerts/AlertRef.cs,Jobs/JobRef.cs,Workers/WorkerRef.cs}]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1062.severity = none

# CA1805: two documented defaults that happen to coincide with the CLR zero. SqlProviderOptions'
# ApplyMigrationsOnStartup = false is the one option on that type whose default is a policy statement
# - its doc comment spends four lines saying production should keep DB lifecycle in infrastructure -
# and it sits directly under DeadlockRetryAttempts = 5, which states its default the same way and is
# not flagged. JobPayloadFormat.None = default is the same shape: it declares that the no-payload
# sentinel *is* the zero-id value, the invariant IsNone reads, and it sits directly above
# Json = BuiltIn(1, "json"). Taking the initializer off either one makes the sibling declarations in
# one block disagree about whether a default is worth writing down, and removes the line a reader
# checks the documented default against.
[src/Acta/{Configuration/SqlProviderOptions.cs,Payloads/JobPayloadFormat.cs}]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1805.severity = none

# CA1716: UpdateOverridesAsync's 'overrides' parameter, which collides with VB's Overrides keyword.
# The word is load-bearing across the three contract tiers docs/internals/naming-conventions.md
# freezes: the feature is operator policy overrides, the argument's own type is
# JobDefinitionPolicyOverrides, the schema spells the modifier _override on every column it qualifies,
# and the method is named for it. Renaming the parameter alone would leave one link in that chain
# calling it something else, which is exactly the drift the naming rules were written to stop - and
# the member is on the frozen 1.0.0 surface, where a rename is a break, not a cleanup.
[src/Acta/Definitions/IDefinitions.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1716.severity = none

# CA1024: GetBehavior(), which CA1024 wants as a property. It is the one member of that extension
# block that throws - its switch closes with ArgumentOutOfRangeException for a code outside the
# family - and .NET's own property guidance is that a getter should not throw. Its two neighbours,
# IsTerminal and ChargesFailureBudget, are total over the enum and are properties for exactly that
# reason; the split follows the guidance rather than ignoring it.
[src/Acta/Execution/ExecutionStatusCode.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1024.severity = none

# CA2225: the implicit widening from JobContract<TInput, TResult> to JobContract<TInput>, which drops
# the result type so one generated member drives both RunAndWaitAsync and the fire-and-forget
# EnqueueAsync. Both sides are readonly record structs over the identical (Type, string) pair, so the
# conversion is total, allocation-free and cannot throw - there is no failure mode a named alternate
# could report differently. Adding ToJobContract() would put a second public spelling of a
# field-for-field copy on a type the manifest generator emits once per declared job, and the type is
# on the frozen 1.0.0 surface.
[src/Acta/Jobs/JobContract.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA2225.severity = none

# CA1711: JobHandlerInvokeDelegate is a delegate declaration, so the suffix reports what the type is.
# CA1711's reserved-suffix list exists to stop a type borrowing a word it does not earn; this one
# earns it, and the name distinguishes the dispatch delegate from the generated invoker it points at.
# Public and frozen at 1.0.0, so a rename is a break.
[src/Acta/Jobs/JobHandlerInvokeDelegate.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1711.severity = none

# CA2225: the two implicit conversions into JobLookup, from JobRef and from JobEnqueueOutcome. The
# friendly alternates CA2225 asks for already exist and are what the operators call - ByRef(JobRef)
# and ById(long) - so the rule is satisfied in substance and fails only on the spelling: it wants
# ToJobLookup / FromJobRef. Acta names lookup factories By* as a family - ByRef, ById,
# ByDeduplicationKey - which reads at the call site as the sentence it is, and the type is on the
# frozen 1.0.0 surface, so a second public name for each would be added and never removed.
[src/Acta/Jobs/JobLookup.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA2225.severity = none

# CA1711: JobBehaviorDelegate is a delegate declaration, on the same reasoning as
# JobHandlerInvokeDelegate's - the suffix is accurate, and here it also separates the continuation
# from the IJobPipelineBehavior that receives it.
# CA1716: the 'next' parameter, which collides with VB's Next keyword. It is the name every .NET
# pipeline gives its continuation, starting with ASP.NET Core's own
# IMiddleware.InvokeAsync(HttpContext, RequestDelegate next) - so the two rules together would have
# Acta rename the exact shape the framework it hosts in ships, and readers would meet a middleware
# chain whose continuation is called something else. Both the delegate and the interface member are
# public and frozen at 1.0.0.
[src/Acta/Jobs/JobPipelineBehavior.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1711.severity = none
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1716.severity = none

# CA1815: JobPayload deliberately does not define what two payloads being equal means. The struct is
# a (format, buffer) pair in transit, and its two candidate meanings are both wrong: the inherited
# ValueType.Equals compares the ReadOnlyMemory field, which is equal when two payloads point at the
# same buffer and length rather than when their bytes match, and a content comparison would be an
# O(n) scan over a buffer that
# JobsOptions.MaxInlinePayloadBytes lets reach 1 MiB by default and 256 MB by configuration, on the
# type every input, result, step and checkpoint body flows through. Nothing in src or tests compares
# payloads, keys a dictionary by one, or puts one in a set; format identity is what code actually
# tests, and JobPayloadFormat carries equality for that.
[src/Acta/Payloads/JobPayload.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1815.severity = none

# CA1031: the group's endpoint filter is this API's last backstop and answers every unhandled failure as
